oach to construct text-based time-series indices in an optimal way\u2014typically, indices that maximize the contemporaneous relation or the predictive performance with respect to a target variable, such as inflation. Our methodology relies on binary selection matrices that, applied to the vocabulary of tokens, select the relevant texts in the corpus. Various widely known text-based indices, such as the Economic Policy Uncertainty (EPU) index, can be formulated in terms of selection matrices. We design a genetic algorithm with domain-specific knowledge featuring tailor-made crossover and mutation operations to perform the complex optimization. We illustrate our methodology with a corpus of news articles from the Wall Street Journal by optimizing text-based indices that forecast inflation at various horizons.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.4830848","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,5,17]],"date-time":"2024-05-17T10:59:31Z","timestamp":1715943571000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Optimal Text-Based Time-Series Indices"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2823-782X","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"David","family":"Ardia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2990-4807","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Keven","family":"Bluteau","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","reference":[{"issue":"3","key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"512","DOI":"10.1111\/joes.12370","article-title":"Econometrics meets sentiment: An overview of methodology and applications","volume":"34","author":"A Algaba","year":"2020","journal-title":"Journal of Economic Surveys"},{"issue":"3","key":"ref2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"817","DOI":"10.2307\/2938229","article-title":"Heteroskedasticity and autocorrelation consisten